<%# Test for Markdown to Typst conversion %>
<%#
  Image conversion is checked as generated markup rather than compiled output:
  the renderer compiles from a temp dir with `--root` set to that dir, so an
  #image() pointing at a repo fixture is unresolvable at compile time.
%>
<% markdown_content = <<~MD
  # Main Heading
  ## Second Level
  ### Third Level

  This is a paragraph with **bold text** and *italic text*.

  Here's a [link](https://typst.app) to Typst.

  - List item 1
  - List item 2
  - List item 3

  `inline code` example

  More __bold__ and _italic_ variations.
MD
%>

= Markdown Conversion Test

<%= markdown_to_typst(markdown_content) %>

== Testing Individual Conversions

Headers:
<%= markdown_to_typst("# H1\n## H2\n### H3\n#### H4\n##### H5\n###### H6") %>

Emphasis:
<%= markdown_to_typst("**bold** and *italic* and __also bold__ and _also italic_") %>

Links:
<%= markdown_to_typst("[Typst Website](https://typst.app)") %>

Images (shown as generated markup, not compiled):

#raw(<%= markdown_to_typst("![Alt text](logo.png)").dump %>, lang: "typst")

Code:
<%= markdown_to_typst("Here is `some code` inline") %>

This document tests Markdown to Typst syntax conversion.
